.resources/TASK-260715-13labb/TASK-260715-13labb_review-results.md-4-
.resources/TASK-260715-13labb/TASK-260715-13labb_review-results.md:5:The implementation matches the macOS-only error-boundary acceptance criteria. It provides stable stage/code/action/retry projections; preserves typed internal mapping evidence for tests; keeps profile, host-policy, credential, and authentication gates terminal; distinguishes bounded transient transport classes without reconnect behavior; keeps cancellation/user stop separate; redacts arbitrary underlying text and prohibited identifiers; and integrates the bounded diagnostic into runtime snapshots. The layering fits the project: platform-neutral taxonomy and snapshot storage are in ReluxTunnelCore, while NWError and OSStatus normalization remain in ReluxTunnelMacOSAdapter. Production bootstrap composition remains correctly deferred to TASK-260715-3t2v9w.
.resources/TASK-260715-13labb/TASK-260715-13labb_review-results.md-6-
.resources/TASK-260715-13labb/TASK-260715-13labb_review-results.md-7-Independent verification:
.resources/TASK-260715-13labb/TASK-260715-13labb_review-results.md:8:- swift test --filter SSHBootstrapErrorMappingTests: exit 0; 10 tests.
.resources/TASK-260715-13labb/TASK-260715-13labb_review-results.md-9-- swift test --filter MacOSSystemKeychainCredentialResolverTests && swift test --filter LibSSH2BridgeTests && swift test --filter LibSSH2AdapterIntegrationTests: exit 0; 13 + 18 + 23 tests.
.resources/TASK-260715-13labb/active-macos-bootstrap-error-mapping-scope.md:1:Implement the stable macOS-only bootstrap error boundary against the accepted profile snapshot loader, system-domain Keychain resolver, mandatory approved-host policy, and selected libssh2 adapter. Keep internal typed causes testable while public/provider diagnostics expose only stable stage, code, user-action category, retry disposition, and bounded non-identifying context. Never expose hostnames, addresses, usernames, profile IDs, Keychain service/account/reference values, raw host keys, fingerprints unless the accepted contract explicitly permits the canonical approved fingerprint for user action, server banners, shell text, private-key material, stack traces, or arbitrary underlying descriptions. Preserve ordering: profile/path/connect/key-exchange/host-policy failures occur before credentials; credential/auth failures occur only after approved host identity. First-use, changed, revoked, unsupported, malformed, corrupt profile, unavailable credentials, and authentication rejection are configuration-or-trust gated rather than blind-retry failures. Cancellation and explicit user stop remain distinct and non-security-labelled. Record transient classifications for later M3 lifecycle work but do not add reconnect behavior. Use Swift Testing golden/redaction tests and selected-engine live or injected evidence where behavior depends on libssh2.
