EPIC-260715-2qzczm_resilience-and-performance/STORY-260715-19ii11_performance-and-resource-tuning/TASK-260721-2ohf99_implement-m3-evidence-bundle-validator-reporter/README.md-9-## Acceptance Criteria
EPIC-260715-2qzczm_resilience-and-performance/STORY-260715-19ii11_performance-and-resource-tuning/TASK-260721-2ohf99_implement-m3-evidence-bundle-validator-reporter/README.md:10:1. The validator accepts only protocol-v1 rows and bundles that contain every required device, environment, revision, server, algorithm, profile, policy, parameter, traffic, impairment, schedule, metric, counter, raw-reference, privacy, authority, gate and review field, with explicit unavailable objects rather than omitted or guessed values. 2. Artifact validation verifies bundle-relative logical references, byte lengths and SHA-256; requires capture authorization, privacy class, retention and redaction evidence; rejects absolute user paths, prohibited fields, unreferenced files, missing restricted-custodian metadata and manifest mutation. 3. The reporter pairs baseline and candidates by device, row and fixed seed, applies the protocol deterministic bootstrap, multiplicity and practical-effect rules exactly, preserves every valid, red, invalid and unavailable input, and emits material-improvement, neutral-pass or explicit red classifications without post-hoc samples or thresholds. 4. Safety failures for bytes, ordinary DNS fallback, routes, resource or memory bounds, failure behavior, nominal drops, collector overflow or cleanup always produce red and cannot be outweighed by performance or energy; provisional and production-authorized states remain separate. 5. Automated positive, boundary and hostile fixtures cover missing and unknown fields, equality and one-over limits, corrupt hashes, duplicate rows, unauthorized captures, redaction failures, exclusions, reruns, unavailable metrics, zero baselines, noisy comparisons, regressions, safety red rows, deterministic replay and immutable accepted-update lineage, and publish task-scoped verification evidence.
