.resources/TASK-260715-27uz4n/TASK-260715-27uz4n_reviewer-focus.md:1:Fresh independent review of the entire portable relay toolchain task. Verify every compiler, Go internal linker, SDK/sysroot policy, target triple, CPU baseline, archive URL/hash, module/source/license hash, runtime assumption, and CI action is exact and source-backed. Audit sanitized environments for host HOME/cache/path/credentials leakage and prove clean mode deletes its target workspace while incremental mode reuses only that isolated workspace. Reproduce missing/tampered input fail-closed behavior, offline Go resolution settings, one documented command per target, four-target clean builds, byte-identical second builds, linkage/runtime inspection, and license extraction. Review CI network boundaries carefully: only approved checksum-pinned fetches may use network; builds must not resolve floating inputs. Confirm macOS 12 and Linux kernel 4.4 claims are proven by binary inspection rather than documentation alone, and that native runtime rows not executable on this host are described honestly without overstating AC. Check the checkout action pin and any version change for correctness. Run Python tests, black, shellcheck, actionlint/YAML, toolchain negative/CI gates, full relay-shell validation, diff/privacy/board gates. Return exactly one verdict and attach task-scoped evidence; do not modify implementation.
