.resources/TASK-260715-2ywde4/TASK-260715-2ywde4_reviewer-focus.md:1:Perform a fresh adversarial review of the complete implementation, not a confirmation of producer claims. Reproduce exact invocation rejection including reordered/duplicated/aggregate-oversized arguments and stable exit codes. Verify protocol stdout is byte-clean for accepted and rejected paths and stderr never includes payload, domain, destination, credential, stdin, executable path, or injected error text. Independently hash the produced Darwin arm64 and Rosetta amd64 executable bytes and compare canonical bounded identity output; exercise mismatch/tamper fixtures and build-variable validation. Scrutinize the Darwin inherited-fd lifecycle: prove malformed hello, CLOSE_SESSION, EOF, SIGINT, SIGTERM, closed stdout, and peer close terminate the process without orphaned children, runtime files, listener sockets, or unbounded goroutine/resource growth; reject a test-only os.Exit shortcut that hides library leaks. Inspect partial reads/writes, timer/join behavior, cancellation races, and descriptor ownership. Re-run pinned Go test/vet, protocol conformance, four-target build metadata, release verify, native/Rosetta identity+stdio smoke, shell/Python/diff/privacy/board gates. Preserve honest native Intel/Linux CI-only boundaries. If any finding requires rework, attach an exact verdict and route to to-dev; accept only if all AC and architecture/security invariants are independently demonstrated.
