.resources/TASK-260715-52h8i3/TASK-260715-52h8i3_inputs.md:1:Add fuzz + allocation-bounds tests for the PacketFlowBridge frame parsing (TASK-260715-3o0co4) + HEV datagram path, proving the TASK-260715-p89bdj contract bound: malformed/hostile frames are rejected within BOUNDED memory and never become arbitrary allocations. FUZZ the forward+reverse framing over hostile input: malformed/short/oversized (>4+MTU) AF words, unknown/mismatched families, truncated frames, zero-length datagrams, boundary-straddling batches, adversarial sequences. PROVE: bounded per-frame + aggregate allocation (no unbounded side buffer/queue), monotonic drop counters, no crash/hang/UB, privacy-safe (no packet bytes/destinations in logs). Deterministic + reproducible (seeded); include an allocation-bounds assertion (e.g. peak-allocation ceiling under a hostile corpus). Build + test via swift build/test on macOS; run under ThreadSanitizer where relevant. Pure test-writing over accepted bridge code; if fuzzing reveals a real bug, STOP-THE-LINE with the reproducing seed/case.
