.resources/TASK-260715-zfg9ap/TASK-260715-zfg9ap_review-focus.md:1:Independent adversarial review focus. Do not trust producer test claims; inspect implementation and outcome artifacts against every AC and accepted TASK-260715-1juybj accounting contract. Trace concurrent reservation and release linearization, token deinit behavior, stale generation, ID rollover or ABA risks, open and flow state transitions, session-health changes, queued-byte arithmetic overflow, double finish and late callbacks, exact baseline recovery, and any deadlock or blocking on packet or SSH executors. Confirm immediate pressure rejection cannot create an SSH channel or side queue and that admitted work is not starved by rejected arrivals. Audit RuntimeDiagnostics schema and encoding for fixed cardinality, bounded size, generation correctness, and prohibited destinations, hostname, address, port, payload, credential, flow identifiers, or attacker-controlled labels. Confirm ceilings remain injected and validated against measuredSafeMaximumFlows and HEV session budget without pretending they are final physical values. Re-run focused normal and TSan suites, full core validation, strict format, boundary/privacy guards, git diff check, and board validate. If any AC is not proven, attach a task-scoped verdict with exact reproducer and route to to-dev; accept only if board status becomes done.
.resources/TASK-260715-zfg9ap/TASK-260715-zfg9ap_rework-01.md:1:Rework round 1 must consume TASK-260715-zfg9ap_review-verdict.md and the attached 20-run churn probe. Close every finding without weakening the accepted non-blocking bounded diagnostics contract. The authoritative registry and all exported current-state gauges must converge to exact baseline even when the bounded diagnostics queue drops intermediate events; do not make packet or SSH executors wait, do not make the queue unbounded, and do not mask divergence only in tests. Preserve monotonic aggregate counters with explicit semantics under dropped ingestion, and retain the diagnostics ingestion-drop signal. Make every reservation identifier allocation fail closed before UInt64 wrap can reuse a live or retired ID; prove no ABA, silent replacement, or leaked capacity at exhaustion. Add deterministic coverage for concurrent explicit release versus deinit, duplicate finish/release, late and stale generation callbacks, session-health transitions racing admission, queued-byte sum overflow or saturation, and sustained pressure where admitted flows progress while rejected arrivals create neither side queues nor SSH opens. Re-run the independent churn reproducer enough times to show both registry and exported gauges return to exact baseline, plus focused normal and TSan suites, full validate-core, strict format, boundary/privacy guards, diff check, and board validate. Update task-scoped outcome evidence and route to to-review; stop only if a clean bounded non-blocking reconciliation design is impossible and attach full constraint evidence.
.resources/TASK-260717-2uyfn5/TASK-260717-2uyfn5_reviewer-focus.md:1:Review independently; do not trust producer summaries. Re-fetch only official Sparkle and Apple primary sources and verify exact current Sparkle 2.9.4 release, tag commit, SPM asset checksum, tagged Package.swift, and complete license terms. Verify every cited updater key and exact semantics, especially SURequireSignedFeed with SUVerifyUpdateBeforeExtraction, SUSignedFeedFailureExpirationInterval=0, SUAllowsAutomaticUpdates, consent behavior, sandbox helper/XPC selection, Mach lookup exceptions, archive/export signing, channel/version rules, downgrade removal, and key rotation. Verify Apple TN3134 direct-distribution packet-tunnel system-extension boundary and ensure approval, replacement, restart, active-provider, and reconnect behavior remain physical gates rather than implementation claims. Challenge the new public updates.relux.works origin, cache/publication policy, private-GitHub manual-download split, same-product identity wording, seven-day logs, forward rollback, and two-custodian key policy as explicit product decisions with no hidden credential or unsupported platform guarantee. Confirm ADR-018, platform-distribution, threat model, security claims, README, LOGBOOK, research, downstream handoff, and dependent board notes are mutually consistent; no file may claim self-update is implemented or shipped. Run task-board validate, git diff --check, focused secret/privacy/path/identity scans, and any lightweight source/checksum reproduction needed. Attach a distinct TASK-260717-2uyfn5 review verdict outcome and choose exactly one reviewer status: done only if all AC are proven; analysis for research corrections; to-dev only for implementation corrections; blocked only for a genuine external or human-only boundary.
