EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/README.md-9-## Acceptance Criteria
EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/README.md:10:Gate A0 is deferred off this epic's critical path under ADR-013 and stays required before App Store distribution and iOS submission, where it must have documented evidence; Gate P0 installs a packet-tunnel provider on the physical Apple-silicon Mac; the physical-iPhone row is a named deferred gap under ADR-024, never inferred from Mac results and never a pass; packet bridge/HEV and one SSH engine pass the M0 matrix; open decisions are recorded with reproducible results.
EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2itwz7_apple-platform-intent-gate/README.md-9-## Acceptance Criteria
EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2itwz7_apple-platform-intent-gate/README.md:10:1. A dated evidence dossier cites the controlling Apple sources and describes the complete packet, TCP, SSH, DNS, and exit-host behavior without euphemism. 2. The dossier identifies the TN3120 ambiguity and asks a decision-capable Apple channel a concrete intended-use and distribution question. 3. Gate evidence is one of the accepted forms: written DTS response, entitlement or review feedback for an accurately disclosed prototype, or an approved architecture change that carries packet semantics to a remote VPN endpoint. 4. Reproducible artifacts record submission text, dates, case or review identifiers, responses, redactions, and source revision. 5. A decision record declares pass, fail, or pivot, states constraints and affected downstream work, and leaves production tasks blocked on any negative or ambiguous result.
EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2itwz7_apple-platform-intent-gate/TASK-260715-1o3q6l_compile-gate-a0-primary-source-dossier/README.md-9-## Acceptance Criteria
EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2itwz7_apple-platform-intent-gate/TASK-260715-1o3q6l_compile-gate-a0-primary-source-dossier/README.md:10:1. A TASK-ID-scoped outcome resource lists every primary Apple source with direct URL, access date, relevant requirement in paraphrase, and the architecture behavior it governs. 2. A traceability table covers local HEV TCP termination, SSH direct-tcpip, UDP relay over SSH exec, DNS handling, default routes, endpoint exclusions, and containing-app versus provider ownership. 3. Facts, inferences, unresolved ambiguity, and assumptions are visibly separated. 4. The dossier states why successful local installation is not Gate A0 evidence and enumerates the accepted authoritative evidence routes. 5. Another researcher can reproduce the source review from the recorded references and revision.
EPIC-260715-2mqgvm_viability-and-foundation/STORY-260715-2xnj3v_apple-capability-provisioning/README.md-3-## Description
