EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/README.md:1:# Reproducible relay supply chain, SBOM, and compliance evidence
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/README.md-2-
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/README.md-3-## Description
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/README.md:4:Productize the approved relay toolchain into reproducible release assets, verified Apple-bundle inputs, dependency inventories, SBOMs, notices, vulnerability policy, checksums, provenance, and update or rollback evidence.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/README.md-5-
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/README.md-6-## Scope
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/README.md:7:In scope: pinned relay and dependency revisions, pinned or recorded build containers and toolchains, Linux and macOS x86_64 and arm64 release builds, independent reproducibility checks, protocol and native or emulated smoke tests, file and build identities, SHA-256 manifests, deterministic Apple-bundle selection, SBOM generation, license and third-party notices for HEV, hev-task-system, hev-socks5-core, lwIP, the SSH engine, and relay dependencies, vulnerability and secret scanning, provenance attestations, release staging, and supply-chain rollback. Out of scope: changing protocol semantics, remote install implementation, Apple code signing, notarization, TestFlight, App Review submission, runtime traffic behavior, and silently accepting unpinned inputs or unexplained binary differences.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/README.md-8-
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/README.md-9-## Acceptance Criteria
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/README.md:10:1. Clean pinned builds produce exactly one uniquely named relay asset for each declared OS and architecture and no undeclared network fetch or mutable dependency input. 2. Two isolated builds reproduce each unsigned asset bit-for-bit or fail with a documented, reviewed nondeterminism that is removed before release. 3. A generated manifest binds protocol version, platform, architecture, size, SHA-256, build identity, source revision, dependency lock digest, and toolchain identity; CI and Apple bundle verification reject every mismatch, omission, duplicate, or ambiguous selection. 4. Machine-readable SBOMs and human-readable notices cover every shipped relay, HEV, lwIP, SSH, and transitive dependency with license text, source revision, and distribution obligation. 5. Release assets pass protocol conformance, hostile-input, stdio boundary, native or approved emulated smoke, self-hash, vulnerability, secret, and notice-completeness gates. 6. The release evidence traces source to bundled bytes and records checksums, attestations, scanners, exceptions, update procedure, rollback procedure, and residual risk without storing credentials.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-14flqo_generate-release-relay-manifest-and-checksums/README.md-3-## Description
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-14flqo_generate-release-relay-manifest-and-checksums/README.md:4:Generate the canonical manifest and checksum files that bind every reproducible relay asset to protocol, platform, architecture, byte size, hash, build identity, source, dependencies, and toolchain inputs.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-14flqo_generate-release-relay-manifest-and-checksums/README.md-5-
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-14flqo_generate-release-relay-manifest-and-checksums/README.md-6-## Scope
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-14flqo_generate-release-relay-manifest-and-checksums/README.md:7:In scope: versioned schema, deterministic ordering and serialization, OS and architecture normalization, file names, byte sizes, SHA-256, protocol version, feature set where approved, build identity, source commit, dependency lock digest, toolchain digest, reproducibility run identifiers, and manifest self-digest. Out of scope: signing Apple bundles, runtime handshake implementation, remote install policy, SBOM generation, and accepting hand-edited manifest fields.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-14flqo_generate-release-relay-manifest-and-checksums/README.md-8-
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-1c4l9v_execute-relay-release-asset-validation-matrix/README.md-3-## Description
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-1c4l9v_execute-relay-release-asset-validation-matrix/README.md:4:Validate the exact reproducible relay bytes across all target environments using protocol, hostile-input, stdio-boundary, resource, identity, self-hash, startup, and clean-exit checks.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-1c4l9v_execute-relay-release-asset-validation-matrix/README.md-5-
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-1z8ac2_document-relay-update-rollback-and-incident-runbook/README.md-6-## Scope
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-1z8ac2_document-relay-update-rollback-and-incident-runbook/README.md:7:In scope: change intake, compatibility and protocol gates, pin updates, license review, rebuild and reproducibility, manifest and SBOM diff review, scan exceptions, staging promotion, Apple-bundle consumers, rollback to prior known-good assets, vulnerable or compromised release withdrawal, attestation trust rotation, retention, communications, owners, and rehearsal. Out of scope: runtime remote upgrade implementation, production traffic operations, Apple store rollback details, and vague advice without commands or decision criteria.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-1z8ac2_document-relay-update-rollback-and-incident-runbook/README.md-8-
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-28y0uc_produce-relay-provenance-and-release-staging-bundle/README.md-6-## Scope
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-28y0uc_produce-relay-provenance-and-release-staging-bundle/README.md:7:In scope: staging directory or archive layout, artifact digests, SLSA-compatible or approved provenance predicate, builder and invocation identity, input materials, reproducibility evidence, manifest and SBOM digests, notices, scan summaries, test evidence, attestation signing through approved keyless or protected mechanism, access control, retention, and downstream verification. Out of scope: Apple code signing, public release publication, embedding production credentials, and rebuilding relay bytes during Apple workflows.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-28y0uc_produce-relay-provenance-and-release-staging-bundle/README.md-8-
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-28y0uc_produce-relay-provenance-and-release-staging-bundle/README.md-9-## Acceptance Criteria
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-28y0uc_produce-relay-provenance-and-release-staging-bundle/README.md:10:1. Staging contains exactly the four verified assets plus canonical manifest, checksums, SBOM, notices, scan and test summaries, reproducibility record, and provenance attestations with deterministic names. 2. Each attestation binds builder, invocation, immutable source and dependency materials, toolchains, subject digests, and relevant evidence without private secret values. 3. Downstream verification starts from a trusted attestation root or approved identity, checks every digest and schema, and rejects missing, extra, replaced, or untrusted content. 4. The Apple release workflows consume staged bytes by digest and cannot rebuild, fetch, or silently substitute relay assets after verification. 5. Tamper, omitted-file, wrong-subject, untrusted-signer, stale-evidence, and retention or access-control fixtures fail staging.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-3c06k7_audit-relay-source-to-staging-compliance-traceability/README.md-6-## Scope
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-3c06k7_audit-relay-source-to-staging-compliance-traceability/README.md:7:In scope: independent digest recomputation, source and dependency material verification, toolchain identity, reproducibility pairs, staging contents, manifest selection rules, protocol identity, SBOM-to-binary reconciliation, notice completeness, scan disposition, attestation verification, exception expiry, Apple archive input expectations, and evidence index. Out of scope: inspecting downstream signed iOS or macOS archives, rebuilding product features, accepting legal risk without owner approval, Apple signature validation, and reviewing runtime tunnel behavior.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-3c06k7_audit-relay-source-to-staging-compliance-traceability/README.md-8-
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-3c06k7_audit-relay-source-to-staging-compliance-traceability/README.md-9-## Acceptance Criteria
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-3c06k7_audit-relay-source-to-staging-compliance-traceability/README.md:10:1. The auditor starts from exact staged bytes and independently verifies hashes, identities, attestations, source and dependency materials, toolchains, and reproducibility evidence. 2. Every binary component maps to the SBOM and notice set and every manifest entry maps to exactly one staged asset with no extras. 3. Protocol and build identities agree across binary output, manifest, provenance, staging metadata, and the declared Apple bundle input contract. 4. All vulnerabilities, license findings, exceptions, and legal reviews are current, scoped, approved, and unexpired at staging time. 5. A TASK-ID-scoped verdict lists pass or fail by requirement, evidence digests, anomalies, residual risk, and exact blockers; downstream Apple archives must consume this accepted staging bundle by digest.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-3e7noa_pin-relay-release-build-environments-and-inputs/README.md-9-## Acceptance Criteria
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-3e7noa_pin-relay-release-build-environments-and-inputs/README.md:10:1. Every source, dependency, generator, toolchain, image, SDK, sysroot, and downloaded archive is addressed by immutable revision and cryptographic digest where supported. 2. A clean bootstrap verifies all digests before use and the actual build can run without resolving mutable branches, tags, latest URLs, or undeclared network inputs. 3. Environment, locale, timezone, paths, compiler flags, linker flags, archive ordering, and build metadata are normalized per the reproducibility contract. 4. The input inventory records licenses and provenance and contains no access tokens, private registry credentials, developer home paths, or private key material. 5. Controlled pin, digest, lock, image, SDK, flag, and undeclared-fetch drift fails before compilation.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-3kepzm_verify-independent-relay-build-reproducibility/README.md:1:# Verify independent bit-for-bit relay build reproducibility
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-19mjyn_relay-supply-chain-and-compliance/TASK-260715-3kepzm_verify-independent-relay-build-reproducibility/README.md-2-
