EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-243sh0_ios-testflight-and-app-store/TASK-260715-1lkgxh_record-ios-source-to-archive-provenance-and-reproducibility/README.md-9-## Acceptance Criteria
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-243sh0_ios-testflight-and-app-store/TASK-260715-1lkgxh_record-ios-source-to-archive-provenance-and-reproducibility/README.md:10:1. Two clean preparations reproduce the approved generated project, dependency graph, relay and resource inputs, version metadata, and every unsigned payload component designated by the contract. 2. Any Apple signing, profile, timestamp, archive-container, or export nondeterminism is identified explicitly and cannot conceal a source, dependency, resource, version, or binary-code difference. 3. Provenance binds source commit, locks, toolchains, build invocation, unsigned input digests, signed archive and export digests, public signing identity, profiles, versions, and App Store Connect build ID. 4. An independent verifier can start from retained inputs and reports and prove the TestFlight or App Review candidate came from the approved candidate without post-validation rebuild. 5. Dirty source, generator drift, dependency drift, relay mismatch, unsigned payload difference, unknown signed difference, wrong profile, or wrong App Store build ID blocks promotion.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-243sh0_ios-testflight-and-app-store/TASK-260715-3661ps_record-ios-distribution-signing-version-and-testflight-contract/README.md-9-## Acceptance Criteria
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-243sh0_ios-testflight-and-app-store/TASK-260715-3661ps_record-ios-distribution-signing-version-and-testflight-contract/README.md:10:1. A TASK-ID-scoped matrix lists every bundle path, identifier, profile, entitlement, version, architecture, resource, signing input, export setting, App Store Connect role, TestFlight group, and verification command. 2. Host and extension use matching approved distribution identities and only the minimum packet-tunnel, App Group, Keychain, and related capabilities traced to Gate P0. 3. Marketing version, monotonic build number, relay protocol and build identity, archive, export, TestFlight build, and later App Review binary are one traceable candidate with no rebuild between channels. 4. Signed-output nondeterminism is distinguished from reproducible source, dependency, generated-project, unsigned-payload, and resource inputs. 5. Platform, security, release, product, and App Store owners approve the contract or disputed signing, group, version, or channel choices remain explicit blockers.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-243sh0_ios-testflight-and-app-store/TASK-260715-3dno4w_inspect-ios-profiles-entitlements-bundle-and-architectures/README.md-9-## Acceptance Criteria
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-243sh0_ios-testflight-and-app-store/TASK-260715-3dno4w_inspect-ios-profiles-entitlements-bundle-and-architectures/README.md:10:1. The verifier enumerates every signed bundle and executable and compares identifiers, Team ID, distribution profiles and expiry, entitlements, extension point, containment, versions, architectures, and deployment targets to the approved matrix. 2. get-task-allow, wildcard identifiers, development profiles, extra App Groups or Keychain groups, unrelated capabilities, missing packet-tunnel rights, and host-extension mismatches fail. 3. Relay resources, privacy manifests, notices, symbols inventory, and unexpected nested frameworks or executables are checked by digest and policy. 4. Results are machine-readable, redacted, reproducible, and retained with public certificate and profile metadata but no private key or issuer material. 5. Negative fixtures cover swapped or expired profile, wrong team, extra entitlement, missing group, wrong extension point, version mismatch, unsupported architecture, tampered resource, and undeclared code.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/README.md-3-## Description
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/README.md:4:Create the operational control plane and evidence package that promotes verified relay, macOS, and iOS candidates, publishes truthful privacy and legal material, supports review with reproducible self-hosted SSH setup, submits the iOS app, and permits safe rollback or response.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/README.md-5-
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/README.md-6-## Scope
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/README.md:7:In scope: release version manifest and go or no-go control, role separation and approvals, cross-platform release and rollback runbooks, current Apple guidance revalidation, public privacy policy and in-app parity, App Privacy labels, export-compliance and regional VPN licensing or storefront decisions, support and retention statements, App Review data-flow and entitlement-purpose evidence, degraded-mode and system-exclusion disclosure, user-owned SSH exit explanation, non-production review host or reproducible setup, review account or profile handling, metadata and screenshot evidence, release-candidate matrix, behavior-to-claim traceability, submission, response handling, incident and credential revocation, and durable audit evidence. Out of scope: inventing legal advice, changing product behavior to match unsupported claims, sharing production credentials, launching unsupported regions, implementing tunnel features, or bypassing negative Gate A0, P0, signing, TestFlight, privacy, or regression evidence.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/README.md-8-
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/README.md-9-## Acceptance Criteria
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/README.md:10:1. A versioned release manifest and runbook identify candidate commits and artifacts, owners, approvals, required CI gates, promotion order, communication, retention, abort criteria, rollback, revocation, and post-release checks for relay, macOS, and iOS. 2. A currently dated primary-source review plus accountable product, privacy, legal, security, and regional approvals produce public policy, App Privacy labels, export-compliance answers, retention or deletion commitments, and storefront availability that match actual behavior. 3. The App Review package accurately explains the VPN data path, Network Extension purpose, user-owned SSH exit, observer boundaries, system exclusions, full and degraded modes, diagnostics, support data, and regional limits without claiming anonymity or a Relux-operated exit service. 4. Reviewers receive a reproducible test profile or isolated SSH host and instructions that exercise the submitted binary without exposing private production credentials; access is scoped, monitored for abuse, rotated, and removed after review. 5. The exact signed candidates pass the supported simulator, physical iPhone, Apple-silicon Mac, accessibility, privacy, leak, lifecycle, entitlement, notarization, TestFlight, artifact, migration, install, upgrade, and rollback matrix, with failures blocking promotion. 6. Submission metadata, screenshots, privacy and support URLs, binary and build identifiers, reviewer notes, communications, rejections, corrections, and resubmissions are preserved and traceable to the reviewed behavior and evidence revision.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/TASK-260715-1kpnkl_provision-isolated-app-review-ssh-test-environment/README.md-3-## Description
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/TASK-260715-1kpnkl_provision-isolated-app-review-ssh-test-environment/README.md:4:Provide a reproducible, least-privilege SSH exit fixture for App Review that exercises host verification, authentication, relay upload or compatible mode, TCP, DNS, UDP where supported, diagnostics, and degraded behavior without exposing production infrastructure or credentials.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/TASK-260715-1kpnkl_provision-isolated-app-review-ssh-test-environment/README.md-5-
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/TASK-260715-1kpnkl_provision-isolated-app-review-ssh-test-environment/README.md-6-## Scope
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/TASK-260715-1kpnkl_provision-isolated-app-review-ssh-test-environment/README.md:7:In scope: dedicated host or reproducible setup, supported OS and OpenSSH, isolated account, public-key authentication, approved host-key fingerprints, no agent forwarding, bounded disk, process, channel, bandwidth and destination controls consistent with product testing, relay directory permissions, logging limited to operational security without traffic payloads, credential delivery through approved review fields, rotation, expiry, abuse monitoring, health checks, teardown, synthetic destinations, and owner runbook. Out of scope: shared production exit credentials, server scanning, public marketplace, inbound unsolicited relay, collecting reviewer traffic content, hardcoded app secrets, and indefinite access.
EPIC-260715-w5gzf4_release-and-distribution/STORY-260715-2dtdql_release-operations-privacy-and-review/TASK-260715-1kpnkl_provision-isolated-app-review-ssh-test-environment/README.md-8-
