EPIC-260716-3fyjn0_manual-validation-and-approvals/STORY-260716-2e86nb_m3-physical-validation/TASK-260715-ixevcp_run-final-m3-resilience-performance-matrix/README.md:10:1. A TASK-ID-scoped matrix records every protocol field, final configuration, raw artifact reference, automated and physical result, pass, red, or unavailable status, owner, and reproduction command for all required rows. 2. Byte and protocol integrity pass, nominal runs have no ordinary loss, induced pressure remains bounded, routes have no loop or broad bypass, and ordinary DNS or application traffic never falls back outside disclosed platform exceptions. 3. Lane policies meet recorded control and throughput baselines, rekeys survive mixed multi-gigabyte traffic, and memory footprint, peak, queues, windows, sessions, associations, overlap, and pressure actions remain within accepted ceilings without avoidable jetsam. 4. Path, endpoint, NAT64, sleep or wake, captive, relay loss, QUIC, and both route modes publish truthful states, fail promptly where required, restore current generations, and clean resources across repeated cycles. 5. The publication names accepted device and OS baselines, parameter values, statistical thresholds, energy and performance regressions, red or unavailable rows, conditional HEV disposition, follow-up task IDs, and privacy-safe raw evidence locations.
