.resources/TASK-260715-24icoz/TASK-260715-24icoz_rework-01-review-results.md-8-
.resources/TASK-260715-24icoz/TASK-260715-24icoz_rework-01-review-results.md:9:`write_portable_asset_archive` uses the predictable sibling path `.<archive>.tmp` and opens it with ordinary `Path.open("wb")` without rejecting a pre-existing symlink or creating the file exclusively. An isolated reviewer reproducer pre-created `.archive.tar.gz.tmp -> victim.txt`, then invoked the public `archive-assets` command. The command exited 0, changed the victim SHA-256 from `bd56300ba5f8e2263128ac97c6852ea42770644808a14d54a04113f23200deb6` to the archive SHA-256 `1f0ba226ed591d1baf5f9464b33e45b7658a33bf5a1a114e77b6d22d3d9eef4e`, and left `archive.tar.gz` as a symlink to `victim.txt`.
.resources/TASK-260715-24icoz/TASK-260715-24icoz_rework-01-review-results.md-10-
.resources/TASK-260715-24icoz/TASK-260715-24icoz_rework-02-review-results.md-8-
.resources/TASK-260715-24icoz/TASK-260715-24icoz_rework-02-review-results.md:9:The rework fully closes the predictable temporary-path symlink vulnerability. `write_portable_asset_archive` now creates an exclusive randomized regular file in the archive destination directory with `tempfile.mkstemp`, writes through the returned owned descriptor, records its device/inode identity, atomically replaces the destination, verifies the destination with `follow_symlinks=False`, and cleans up only a still-regular path whose device/inode matches the invocation-owned temporary file.
.resources/TASK-260715-24icoz/TASK-260715-24icoz_rework-02-review-results.md-10-
--
.resources/TASK-260715-24icoz/TASK-260715-24icoz_rework-02-review-results.md-14-- The created temporary name was randomized (`.archive.tar.gz.<random>.tmp`), in the destination directory, and a regular file at replacement time.
.resources/TASK-260715-24icoz/TASK-260715-24icoz_rework-02-review-results.md:15:- A pre-existing final archive symlink was rejected with `portable archive output must be a regular file`; its victim was unchanged.
.resources/TASK-260715-24icoz/TASK-260715-24icoz_rework-02-review-results.md-16-- On injected `os.replace` failure, a temporary pathname replaced by another actor remained present with its foreign inode/bytes, proving cleanup does not unlink a path it no longer owns.
