.resources/TASK-260715-3bdplx/TASK-260715-3bdplx_inputs.md:1:Select the relux-relay implementation language + cross-build toolchain. This portable rootless executable runs on the user EXIT HOST (Linux and macOS, x86_64 and arm64) and speaks the relay protocol over the SSH exec/stdio channel (UDP-over-SSH per ADR-005/006, no SFTP). Per .spec/relay-protocol.md, security-privacy.md (relay supply chain), platform-distribution.md. EVALUATE at least Swift, Go, and Rust/C-family against: portability (static/near-static linking, minimal libc/runtime deps; musl for Linux static), binary size, memory footprint, build reproducibility, testing story, security/supply-chain (SBOM, pinning), and maintenance. AC REQUIRES a minimal hello-stdio + UDP capability PROOF (or equivalent primary evidence) validating EVERY required OS/arch claim — actually cross-build and run the tiny proof where feasible; if a target cannot be cross-built in this environment, record the exact toolchain gap as a blocking item (stop-the-line), do NOT claim unverified support. Decide: language, compiler/toolchain versions, dependency policy, target triples, output names, checksum/manifest format. Output must let the dependent target-shell (1ccx3l) and native-dep seams (1g9cyt) proceed without a tooling question. Consumers: TASK-260715-1ccx3l, 1g9cyt, and the M2 relay build.
