LOGBOOK.md:786:- OWNERSHIP: Handshake, flow, and opening tokens provide once-only release plus deinit rollback. Flow termination atomically releases an in-flight open, owned channel, reserved/live bytes, and phase slot before publishing one finite terminal reason. A late open completion after terminal cleanup is counted as a discarded event rather than a second release. Existing admitted flows continue byte/buffer progress while new work is rejected under pressure.
LOGBOOK.md:864:- DECISION: Fault injection uses the coordinator's injected cancellation-check seam to fail at fourteen exact before/after ownership boundaries. This keeps production code unchanged while proving reverse rollback, one disconnecting publication, one terminal publication, exact error mapping, and single cleanup for configuration, SSH, TCP, DNS, packet plane, settings, and packet-read ownership.
