+### M5 bundle, compliance, and release gates
+
+The M2 runbook produces unsigned hash-verifiable inputs. These backlog tasks
+own later validation and release boundaries: `TASK-260715-1c4l9v` native release
+matrix, `TASK-260715-36gq4m` four-row workflow, `TASK-260715-1lmmri` Apple bundle
+enforcement, `TASK-260715-151xf0` notices, `TASK-260715-37rtzn` SBOM,
+`TASK-260715-28y0uc` staging provenance, `TASK-260715-3c06k7` traceability,
+`TASK-260715-3sk5cd` signing, `TASK-260715-387eof` notarization,
+`TASK-260715-1gzhnk` release compliance bundle, and `TASK-260715-312u2k`
+go/no-go approval. `TASK-260715-1z8ac2` will own the broader M5 relay release
+incident runbook; it must consume rather than weaken this M2 byte boundary.
+
+## Handoff checklist
+
+- All four canonical files and the exact manifest were rebuilt from recorded
+  source, recipe, tool, version, protocol, and epoch pins.
+- Two clean builds and normalized archives matched byte-for-byte.
+- Supply-chain, notice, SPDX, provenance, checksum, manifest, native runtime,
+  bundle, Apple integration, and bootstrap consumer results are attached with
+  real exit codes.
+- The known-good rollback archive and metadata remain immutable and retrievable.
+- No standalone signing claim, remote pre-verification execution, credential
+  evidence, local-only native claim, or future backlog gate is represented as a
+  pass.
